# UBSan reports the boot stage (boot_stage.py) does not fail on: known undefined behaviour in engine code that is
# harmless on the ABIs we ship (arm64, x86_64) and waits for its own fix. Every entry names its cause; remove an
# entry with its fix. A new report anywhere else, or of another kind, fails the stage.

# The technique parser steps a char pointer that is null for empty sources (technique.cpp:1487, 1625).
pointer-overflow:src/libs/renderer/src/technique.cpp
# The BSP ray test keeps its stack pointer one before the array and pre-increments it (collide.cpp:37-38).
bounds:src/libs/geometry/src/collide.cpp
# bimg's KTX writer advances its source pointer while it measures a texture with no pixel data (texture/core/cache.cpp
# write_ktx with a sizer; bimg image.cpp
# imageWriteKtx; third-party, pin bimg in engine/pins.json).
pointer-overflow:storm_bimg-*/src/image.cpp
# ncnn's x86 im2col convolution leaves its k-tile scratch empty when the whole K fits one tile (K <= TILE_K, by design:
# the sums go straight to the output) and still advances that null scratch pointer, never writing through it
# (convolution_im2col_gemm.h, `outptr += ...` in convolution_gemm_transB_packed_tile; third-party, pin ncnn in
# engine/pins.json).
pointer-overflow:storm_ncnn-*/src/layer/x86/convolution_im2col_gemm.h
